{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793600321,"nonce":"bjttAVjby4bo4bdeC7VRCZ7XQ7Q=","title":"The second half of the old M5, split off during the 2026-11-01 roadmap review so the first end-to-end result (M5a) doesn't wait on the server, cache and store. Depends on M5a.","message":"- `leansharp-server` (net10.0, design §8.1): JSON-RPC over named pipe / Unix socket; `verify`, `cancel`, `status`, `explain`, `export`, `report`; per-unit fuel and wall-clock limits (budgets from §12 Q8, decided when M5a starts).\n- Content-addressed cache (design §8.2) keyed on canonical VIR, dependency statements, bundle/environment hashes (including the attribute sidecar) and kernel version; certificates can be re-checked by the kernel alone (`LeanSharpRecheck=true`).\n- Store v1 (design §7.3): versioned binary format, content-addressed blobs, name index, memory-mapped reads, manifest. Trusted vs verified import modes (design §7.2). The Mathlib run's memory figure should inform the layout.\n- The MSBuild task switches from the in-process engine to the server.\n- CLI grows `check-store`, `import`, `explain` (design §3.2).\n- `LeanSharp.Analyzers`: deterministic checks only, no I/O.\n\n\nThe M5a result through the server. A second build is served from the cache without running tactics; `LeanSharpRecheck=true` re-checks cached certificates with the kernel alone; the Init + semantics store passes `leansharp check-store` in verified mode. Baseline per-unit verification latency and server memory are recorded for M8.\n\nStatus: not started.","files":null}]}